WEBVTT

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.170
I knew it was old...

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:15.210
The connectors use a generations-old
standard, you see. Still...

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.250
600 years old?
That makes my head hurt...

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.350
You never noticed anything when
you were tinkering with her?

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.150
Why would I think about something
like that while I'm working?!

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.360
I always stay focused, you know!

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.400
Strains were first developed
only 150 years ago...

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.270
I hear Mimics were developed
much earlier than that, but...

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.640
This must be one of
the very first ones, then...

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.440
So, the enemy's constant attacks
are aimed at getting this?

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.180
That, we don't know for sure.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.780
I'd like to open it now. That alright?

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.110
Please do.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.620
I've heard that there's
nothing wrong with Sara.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.620
Which means there's something
about this that we don't know.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.850
I never got the chance to closely
examine her and Sara, you see...

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:07.130
--What?!
--My word...

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.930
What? What is it?

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.300
This isn't a human brain!

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.340
Then, what is it?

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.410
Just what kind of brain is it, then?!

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.850
She linked with that thing?!

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.010
No wonder it acts differently!

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:31.560
Sara didn't link with this!
It probably linked with her!

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.030
Memories of the Future

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:44.260
There is no creature we know
of that has a brain like this!

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.360
Then, you're suggesting...

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:49.830
...that this is from an alien?

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:52.500
Most likely, if that's
the only possibility...

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.770
But the more pressing question
is why this thing even exists.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:01.110
If the Deague knows about this,
I don't blame them for wanting it.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.080
Looks like I'll need to do
a detailed examination.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.220
Gimme a hand, Ben! Carmichael!

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.620
No... No...

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.550
No!

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.160
What is it?

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.660
It's her! Help her!

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.800
Help her!

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.800
Help... Hurry!

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.140
Help!

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.210
Help!

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.910
Help... her!

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.150
If we don't hurry...

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.980
I know...

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.480
Our time's up.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.890
If we don't finish our course
change by 1200 tomorrow

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.590
and rendezvous with the main fleet,

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:50.260
we won't make it in time
for the next operation.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.660
In other words, we can't
get sidetracked anymore.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.330
I guarantee your status.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.800
We've gained a part of instant
interstellar communication technology.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.440
I won't let anyone question you.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.510
I'll protect you. Don't you worry.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:11.500
I'm going to use the shower first.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.820
What?!

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.330
It won't open!

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.700
What are you doing, Ralph?!

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.700
Hey! Ralph?! Ralph!

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:44.880
You...

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:49.450
Come to complain, have you?
But you're too late.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:52.820
Until now, you've always had
your way. But from now on-

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.490
I'm closing in!
I should see it any moment now!

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.930
There it is! The target!

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.400
No sign of the enemy! Making contact!

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:46.340
The hull appears to have
taken considerable damage!

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.780
What was that?!

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:57.450
Was that the new enemy model
we heard about?!

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:06.830
They're almost like Strains!

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.700
When did the Deague suddenly get these?!

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.840
Only one left!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.140
Only one left!

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.920
N-no! Help!

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.150
What?!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:46.790
A person?! They're not unmanned?!

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:55.610
A k-kid...

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:56.840
A kid?!

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.490
Stay in the room...

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.930
Get out.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:54.940
--At least let me get dressed...
--I disposed of your clothes.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:55.930
Eh?

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:04.640
I see. You disposed of everything
that might have my ID on it.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:12.920
A single towel? What if someone sees me?

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.010
There is no one left to see you.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.180
Ralph... don't tell me you-

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.750
What have you done?

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:44.920
You will continue our pursuit.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:48.860
One person should be able
to pilot this ship.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.630
Quickly, there is no time to waste.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:57.870
Yes, that's right.
One person can pilot the Kunrun.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:03.170
I'm even skilled enough to conduct
sub-light speed travel by myself!

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.410
But, that doesn't mean you had to-

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:09.380
Why? Why did this have to happen?!

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.280
What did I ever do?!

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:17.320
I'm on your side! I've helped
you in every way possible!

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:20.560
So why are you doing this?! Why?!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.550
Why, Ralph?!

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.370
Ten seconds to acceleration start.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:37.610
Nine. Eight. Seven. Six. Five.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:40.580
Four. Three. Two.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.070
Commencing acceleration!

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:54.720
We are now traveling at sub-light
speed toward Planet Bregma,

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.260
our original destination.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.130
We are scheduled to arrive
in two days' ship time.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:05.200
Union forces there should be
conducting large-scale exercises.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:08.940
After consulting with the
high-level military officials there

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.780
and re-supplying, repairing,
and performing other needed measures,

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.380
we plan to return home.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.750
What does "other needed measures" mean?

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:20.820
Sara, obviously.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.750
--W-what's going to happen to her?
--Who knows.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.820
They'll probably just hand her over
and let the army handle the rest.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:31.050
Somethin' just don't feel
right about this...

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:41.930
Okay! All done!

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.240
Do you know what happened to Sara?

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.180
No, I haven't heard anything...

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.880
Damn it!

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:58.420
There've been many casualties
on this incident-plagued voyage,

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:03.260
but I ask that you use this experience
in your post-graduation duties.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.750
That is all I have to say.

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:10.500
Come on, Craven!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.600
I've compromised as far as I can

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:16.040
and analyzed the Mimic in
every way but dissection!

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.700
Surely you can accept such a small request!

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:23.910
As long as it's only until
we reach Bregma...

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.480
Yes! That's the Craven I know!

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.470
Well, I better get to work!

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.420
He's just too much to control...

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:42.790
Get up.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.900
--I brought her.
--Good work.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:52.970
What did you do to Emily?!

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:55.810
We took a look at the Mimic inside her.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:11:00.650
Did you know this Mimic
was created 600 years ago?

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:02.080
You can't be serious...

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:06.790
This would all make sense
if you were born 600 years ago...

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:10.290
But seeing as you're Ralph Werec's sister,
that's out of the question.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:13.850
Emily... Who are you?

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.100
Course prediction complete.

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:24.270
The enemy ship's destination
is Planet Bregma.

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:29.010
After that supply depot incident,
they should know we're following.

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.150
There's something where they're headed.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:33.150
Are we still going anyway?

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.420
Yes.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.020
We're at a disadvantage
if we get in a fight.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.520
Barrow, the second in command,
has the TUMOR activation password.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:45.790
If we can't use TUMORs,
we're as good as unarmed.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.590
I know.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:51.300
What in the hell are you thinking?

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.290
What's driving you to go to such lengths?

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.510
How am I able to link
with a 600-year-old Mimic?

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.710
Strains didn't even exist back then!

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:05.710
That's why I called you here:
to figure that out.

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.580
You want to know too, don't you?

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.380
But...

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:14.320
I believe this Mimic is at
the center of all these incidents.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:17.760
So, I want to investigate
it as much as time allows!

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:21.200
Besides, if we don't learn "who" this is

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.330
you'll never know what it
is your brother wants to do!

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:28.200
You can't move forward by being passive.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:38.150
Listen, we're not just starting
it up this time around.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.880
Your goal is to link even
deeper than usual

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.620
and get any information
you can from the Mimic.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:47.890
Though, I've never done this before,
so I'm not sure what'll happen.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:49.890
Be extra careful.

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:53.660
Activation setup complete.
All sensors OK.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.700
Alright! Let's get to it, then!

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:58.700
Melchi...

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:02.540
Should we tell her the brain
inside Emily isn't human?

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:07.180
I don't plan on telling her for now.
It would only confuse her.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.080
Sara, about to begin.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.270
Right!

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:31.730
Emily?

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:45.550
The link level is too high!
It's three times higher than predicted!

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.550
That's impossible!

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.150
You didn't do anything weird
when you dissected it, did you?!

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:50.490
Of course I-

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:54.580
Wait, is it possible it's
stimulated the memory cortex?!

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:02.490
What is this?

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:11.800
Are these her memories?

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.230
These are...

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.360
Whoa, they all look the same!

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:41.360
Clones? Could they be
the latest Deague weapon?!

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.590
Nieren 6...

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:51.980
6361... Over 600 years ago...

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:55.980
They appear, on the outside,
to be little girls from our world,

00:14:55.980 --> 00:15:00.050
but their internal composition is
fundamentally different from ours.

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:02.220
They're aliens, in simpler terms.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:06.760
So, this is mankind's
very first "first contact"...

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:10.430
Yes, but there's something even
more fascinating than that...

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:14.170
They appear to share
a collective consciousness.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:15.570
Share?

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.240
Yes, and without any time lag.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:20.240
No matter how far apart they are?

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:22.480
Even if they're light-years apart.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.670
That is indeed fascinating...

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:31.090
None of our anesthetics
work on them, do they?

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.120
No, but they're researching it...

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.520
But they all share the same consciousness,

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:38.460
so they'll get used to
being dissected anyways...

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:46.900
Sharing consciousness is synonymous
with sharing information.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:48.970
If we can clarify how this ability works,

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:54.080
we'll have a new means of
communication that changes everything!

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:57.280
Instant communication between
star systems light-years apart

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:59.110
would be possible!

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.450
If we can make this a reality,

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:06.990
it will have great merit
for fleet operations!

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:11.260
That's not all. If instant
communication becomes possible,

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:13.260
it changes everything
we know by suggesting

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.960
it's not impossible to surpass
the speed of light.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:19.130
It would be possible to move
troops faster than light?

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:21.770
It would make distance itself
completely meaningless.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:25.710
In short, instant transportation
would be possible, and...

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.580
Is it usable like this?

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:29.780
This is all that's needed
for instant communication.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.010
Plus, we're low on samples now, so...

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:37.420
You're to be sent to Grabera now.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:41.590
Don't worry, it won't take long
to get there while you sleep.

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:44.290
Oh, yes. I hear they're
working on a weapon

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:47.230
that uses your technology and abilities.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.320
I think they call it
a "Strain" or something?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:55.340
I'm being taken to that planet...

00:16:55.340 --> 00:17:02.140
And I continued to follow me
so that I could take me back...

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.270
Brother...

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:12.120
What was that?!

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:14.780
Was that the new enemy model
we heard about?!

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:22.320
He continued to kill me...

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.730
In the distant future...

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:52.320
Why? Why such-

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.800
How could I... we...

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:06.470
have done something so unforgivable...

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:09.880
My brother learned...

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:13.350
...what he... what the Union people...

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:16.250
...had done to "us"...

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:21.820
How... can I atone...
for something like this?

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.350
You can atone...

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:32.630
If I open the Baxter Gate inside me...

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:35.540
Help her...

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.200
Help!

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.480
We've lost control here!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:51.780
Her mental load's going to hit
the red zone if we don't do something!

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:08.470
Sara! Are you okay?!

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:13.410
Now I see...

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.740
So that's why my brother is...

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:30.560
There.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:33.160
He is a man who betrays his allies.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:38.120
I knew this would happen someday,
but this is where it stops!

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:45.010
I assume the TUMORs will accept
my orders in their current state?

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:48.440
Damn you! You planned this
from the very start?!

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.450
Final deceleration complete.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.920
Synchronization with
objective time complete.

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:06.190
Hailing the stationed fleet.

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:09.630
--It's finally over now...
--Yes.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.830
T-that can't be!

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:12.930
What is it?!

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:15.640
The allied forces...
The allied forces aren't here!

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:18.470
--Impossible!
--Are you certain?!

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:19.310
Yes, sir!

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:23.710
There's not even... not even a single
craft in the planet's vicinity!

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:27.700
What?! How can that be?!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:37.150
He made a heavy promise.
What he bore was atonement.

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:40.920
On the next Soukou no Strain:
"The Beginning of Revelry"

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.610
All of mankind is my brother's enemy.
